## 5. Standard system preflight

Run this before diagnosis or any proposed change.

```sh
HA_CONT="${HA_CONT:-homeassistant}"

echo "===== HOST ====="
date
hostname
uname -a
uptime
df -h

echo "===== DOCKER ====="
docker version --format '{{.Server.Version}}' 2>/dev/null || docker version
docker ps --format 'table {{.Names}}\t{{.Image}}\t{{.Status}}\t{{.Ports}}'

echo "===== HOME ASSISTANT CONTAINER ====="
docker inspect "$HA_CONT" --format '
Name={{.Name}}
Image={{.Config.Image}}
State={{.State.Status}}
StartedAt={{.State.StartedAt}}
Restarting={{.State.Restarting}}
ExitCode={{.State.ExitCode}}
NetworkMode={{.HostConfig.NetworkMode}}
' 2>/dev/null

echo "===== HOME ASSISTANT VERSION ====="
docker exec "$HA_CONT" python -m homeassistant --version 2>/dev/null || true

echo "===== CONFIG MOUNT ====="
docker inspect "$HA_CONT" --format '{{range .Mounts}}{{println .Source "->" .Destination}}{{end}}' 2>/dev/null

echo "===== RECENT LOGS ====="
docker logs --tail=250 "$HA_CONT" 2>&1 | tail -n 250
```

Interpretation:

- If the container is restarting, inspect logs before changing anything.
- If disk is full, fix storage before restarting or updating.
- If `/config` is not mounted or not discoverable, stop and report.
- If Home Assistant version cannot be read, inspect container status and logs.

