## 6. Configuration directory map

Inside the container, Home Assistant sees the config directory as:

```text
/config
```

Common files and directories:

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `/config/configuration.yaml` | Main YAML entry point |
| `/config/automations.yaml` | Common YAML automation storage |
| `/config/scripts.yaml` | Common script storage |
| `/config/scenes.yaml` | Common scene storage |
| `/config/secrets.yaml` | Secret references; not encrypted |
| `/config/home-assistant.log` | Current Home Assistant log file |
| `/config/home-assistant.log.1` | Rotated log |
| `/config/home-assistant_v2.db` | Recorder SQLite database |
| `/config/.storage/` | UI-managed JSON storage and registries |
| `/config/custom_components/` | HACS/custom integrations |
| `/config/packages/` | Optional package-based YAML organization |
| `/config/blueprints/` | Blueprint imports |
| `/config/python_scripts/` | `python_script` integration scripts |
| `/config/www/` | Static files exposed under `/local/` |
| `/config/zigbee.db` | Common ZHA database file, if ZHA is used |
| `/config/esphome/` | ESPHome configs, if stored under HA config |

Host-side paths differ. Discover the host path from Docker mounts.

