## 12. API diagnostics

Use the REST API only with a token from a secure credential broker.

### 12.1 Basic health/config

```sh
curl -fsS -H "Authorization: Bearer $HA_TOKEN" http://127.0.0.1:8123/api/
curl -fsS -H "Authorization: Bearer $HA_TOKEN" http://127.0.0.1:8123/api/config
```

### 12.2 States and services

```sh
curl -fsS -H "Authorization: Bearer $HA_TOKEN" http://127.0.0.1:8123/api/states
curl -fsS -H "Authorization: Bearer $HA_TOKEN" http://127.0.0.1:8123/api/services
```

For large systems, do not paste full API output into chat. Filter locally with `jq` if available.

Examples:

```sh
curl -fsS -H "Authorization: Bearer $HA_TOKEN" http://127.0.0.1:8123/api/states \
  | jq -r '.[] | [.entity_id, .state] | @tsv'
```

### 12.3 Test action carefully

Only call live actions when requested or needed for validation.

```sh
curl -fsS -X POST \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $HA_TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  http://127.0.0.1:8123/api/services/persistent_notification/create \
  -d '{"title":"Agent test","message":"Home Assistant API test succeeded."}'
```

Use harmless tests first. Do not toggle real lights, locks, alarms, garage doors, valves, thermostats, or appliances without approval.

