## 18. Z-Wave JS / Z-Wave JS UI

Z-Wave is usually separated into:

1. Z-Wave JS UI container/server
2. Home Assistant Z-Wave integration connecting to it over WebSocket

Common ports:

- Z-Wave JS UI web interface: often `8091`
- Z-Wave JS WebSocket server: often `3000`

Discovery:

```sh
docker ps --format 'table {{.Names}}\t{{.Image}}\t{{.Status}}\t{{.Ports}}' | grep -i zwave || true
docker logs --tail=300 zwave-js-ui 2>&1
```

If the container name differs, discover it first.

Checks:

```sh
docker inspect "<zwave_container>" --format '{{range .Mounts}}{{println .Source "->" .Destination}}{{end}}'
docker inspect "<zwave_container>" --format '{{json .HostConfig.Devices}}'
ls -l /dev/serial/by-id/ 2>/dev/null
```

Home Assistant logs:

```sh
docker logs --tail=1000 "$HA_CONT" 2>&1 | grep -iE 'zwave|zwave_js|zwave_js_server|websocket' | tail -n 200
```

Rules:

- Do not include/exclude devices without approval.
- Do not change controller path without approval.
- Do not wipe Z-Wave JS UI store.
- Do not disable security keys.
- Back up Z-Wave controller NVM through supported tooling/UI before major controller work.
- If HA cannot connect, check the WebSocket URL, container network, port exposure, and Z-Wave JS UI WS Server setting.

---

## 19. Matter / Thread / OTBR

Matter commonly depends on a separate Matter Server and proper IPv6/mDNS/Thread networking.

Common Matter Server WebSocket pattern:

```text
ws://<matter-server-host>:5580/ws
```

Discovery:

```sh
docker ps --format 'table {{.Names}}\t{{.Image}}\t{{.Status}}\t{{.Ports}}' | grep -i matter || true
docker logs --tail=300 "<matter_container>" 2>&1
```

Home Assistant logs:

```sh
docker logs --tail=1000 "$HA_CONT" 2>&1 | grep -iE 'matter|thread|otbr|border router|mdns|zeroconf|ipv6' | tail -n 250
```

Network checks:

```sh
ip -6 addr show 2>/dev/null || true
ip -6 route show 2>/dev/null || true
docker network ls
docker inspect "<matter_container>" --format '{{.HostConfig.NetworkMode}}'
```

Rules:

- Do not disable IPv6 casually.
- Do not change Docker network mode casually.
- Do not reset Matter fabric without approval.
- Do not remove Matter integration/config entries manually unless following a documented recovery.
- Matter commissioning/removal is an operator-approved action, not a background fix.

