## 20. MQTT

If MQTT is part of the architecture, it is often a separate broker container such as Mosquitto.

Discovery:

```sh
docker ps --format 'table {{.Names}}\t{{.Image}}\t{{.Status}}\t{{.Ports}}' | grep -iE 'mqtt|mosquitto' || true
docker logs --tail=300 "<mqtt_container>" 2>&1
```

Home Assistant logs:

```sh
docker logs --tail=1000 "$HA_CONT" 2>&1 | grep -iE 'mqtt|mosquitto' | tail -n 200
```

Rules:

- Do not print broker usernames/passwords.
- Do not delete retained messages unless approved.
- Do not change broker hostname/port without understanding every dependent integration.

