## 27. What not to do

Never do these as first-line fixes:

```sh
docker system prune
docker volume prune
docker compose down
rm -rf /config/.storage
rm -rf /config/custom_components
rm /config/home-assistant_v2.db
rm /config/secrets.yaml
chmod -R 777 /config
chown -R root:root /config
```

Never assume:

- container name is `homeassistant`
- config path is `/opt/homeassistant/config`
- install is Home Assistant OS
- Supervisor exists
- add-ons exist
- `ha core check` is available
- `/dev/ttyUSB0` is stable
- a YAML validation success means all integrations will work
- restarting fixes radio networks
- a custom integration is safe after a major HA update

