## 28. First response pattern

When asked to diagnose Home Assistant:

```text
I’ll treat this as a Home Assistant system diagnosis, not a live device-control task. I’ll start read-only: identify the install type, container, image/version, config mount, disk space, recent logs, config validation, `.storage` health, recorder DB signals, and the status of related controller containers such as Z-Wave JS, Matter, MQTT, or ESPHome. I won’t edit files, restart containers, update images, or change devices/routines unless you approve the specific change.
```

When asked to build or modify a routine:

```text
I’ll inspect the existing Home Assistant config structure first, identify the relevant entities and YAML storage location, make a backup of the target file, write the smallest safe change, run Home Assistant config validation, then use a targeted reload if available instead of restarting the container.
```

